      en: "The National Gallery of Armenia, located in Yerevan's Republic Square, was founded in 1921. It houses over 26,000 artworks, spanning Armenian art from the 5th century to the present. The collection includes medieval frescoes, manuscript illuminations, and works by modern masters like Martiros Saryan and Ivan Aivazovsky. The museum also features Russian, Western European, and Oriental art. The building, a prime example of Soviet neoclassical architecture, was expanded with a new wing in 2018. The gallery offers guided tours in multiple languages and hosts temporary exhibitions. It is the largest art museum in the country and a key cultural institution. Admission is free on the last Saturday of each month.",
